WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.265
Meet Buffer, a read only explorer for Drift perpetual positions on Solana.

00:00:05.265 --> 00:00:10.180
This walkthrough uses a deterministic sample. Every balance and price you see

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:11.408
here is illustrative.

00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:16.779
The long and short sample holds one hundred SOL long, and half

00:00:16.779 --> 00:00:21.249
a Bitcoin short. Choose a shared ten percent price decline to explore

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:22.367
both positions together.

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:27.998
The SOL position loses fifteen hundred U S D C. The Bitcoin

00:00:27.998 --> 00:00:32.729
short gains five thousand. Together, that is thirty five hundred of incremental

00:00:32.729 --> 00:00:34.700
perpetual price profit and loss.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:40.954
Switch to partial coverage. Buffer keeps the excluded contract, collateral, debt, and

00:00:40.954 --> 00:00:46.308
open orders visible. The modeled result never pretends to include everything in

00:00:46.308 --> 00:00:47.200
the account.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:53.959
Open Method to inspect the calculation and its limits. Position sizes stay

00:00:53.959 --> 00:00:59.819
fixed. Funding, fees, fills, collateral changes, and liquidation effects are outside this

00:00:59.819 --> 00:01:01.283
simple price model.

00:01:02.183 --> 00:01:08.306
Download a JSON report with the sample source, scenario inputs, position contributions,

00:01:08.306 --> 00:01:14.429
exclusions, and assumptions. It is a reproducible explanation of this specific modeled

00:01:14.429 --> 00:01:15.450
price move.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:20.723
The same explorer adapts to a smaller screen. Change the price move

00:01:20.723 --> 00:01:25.097
and review the result. Start with a sample, then explore a public

00:01:25.097 --> 00:01:27.283
account when live reads are configured.
